<section id="assistant" class="scroll-mt-6">
  <% capability_catalog = Assistant::CapabilityCatalog.load %>
  <% capability_tools = capability_catalog.tools.map { |tool| tool.fetch("name") } %>
  <% capability_effects = capability_catalog.tools.map { |tool| tool.fetch("effect") }.uniq.sort %>
  <% capability_modules = capability_catalog.tools.map { |tool| tool.fetch("module") }.uniq.sort %>
  <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4">
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100">Assistant</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Session-only administration for the Hunter assistant. Through the reviewed Hunter MCP catalog, enabled backends have administrator-equivalent operational access: workflow analysis, non-secret create and versioned edit, Whiterabbit job submission, Ansible utilities and launches, cancellation, monitoring, and human-owned exports. Actions are attributed to you and audited. The LLM can never see secrets, delete records, change security governance, or bypass MCP with a generic proxy.</p>
    </div>
    <span class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-medium <%= Assistant::Config.enabled? && setting.assistant_enabled? ? 'bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-700 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300' : 'bg-rose-100 text-rose-700 dark:bg-rose-500/15 dark:text-rose-300' %>">
      <%= Assistant::Config.enabled? && setting.assistant_enabled? ? "Enabled" : "Disabled" %>
    </span>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 p-4 text-sm text-amber-900 dark:border-amber-700 dark:bg-amber-950/30 dark:text-amber-200">
    The database switch and the infrastructure gate must both be enabled. Turning this switch off stops new conversations immediately.
  </div>

  <%= form_with url: api_v1_assistant_settings_path, method: :patch,
    class: "mt-5 grid gap-4 rounded-lg border border-zinc-200 p-4 dark:border-zinc-800",
    data: { turbo: false } do %>
    <label class="flex items-center gap-3 text-sm text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">
      <%= check_box_tag "settings[assistant_enabled]", "1", setting.assistant_enabled?, class: "rounded border-zinc-300" %>
      Enable assistant in Hunter
    </label>
    <%= hidden_field_tag "settings[operational_access_enabled]", "0" %>
    <label class="flex items-center gap-3 text-sm text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">
      <%= check_box_tag "settings[operational_access_enabled]", "1", setting.operational_access_enabled?, class: "rounded border-zinc-300" %>
      Enable reviewed Hunter operational access through MCP
    </label>
    <%= hidden_field_tag "settings[control_center_write_enabled]", "0" %>
    <label class="flex items-center gap-3 text-sm text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">
      <%= check_box_tag "settings[control_center_write_enabled]", "1", setting.control_center_write_enabled?, class: "rounded border-zinc-300" %>
      Enable effectful Control Center operations (authoring, jobs, utilities, launch, cancel, export)
    </label>
    <%= hidden_field_tag "settings[conversation_management_enabled]", "0" %>
    <label class="flex items-center gap-3 text-sm text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">
      <%= check_box_tag "settings[conversation_management_enabled]", "1", setting.conversation_management_enabled?, class: "rounded border-zinc-300" %>
      Enable direct conversation rename and reorder for the signed-in administrator
    </label>

    <div class="rounded-lg border border-zinc-200 bg-zinc-50 p-4 dark:border-zinc-800 dark:bg-zinc-900/50">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100">Live MCP capability controls</h3>
      <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-5 text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
        Selected tools, effects, and modules are disabled immediately, including for active turn grants. The model cannot change these controls. Use Ctrl/Cmd-click to select or clear individual entries.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-5 text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
        Effective defaults: <%= Assistant::Config.max_tool_calls %> tool calls, <%= Assistant::Config.max_effects_per_turn %> effects, and <%= Assistant::Config.max_launches_per_turn %> launches per turn; <%= number_to_human_size(Assistant::Config.max_result_bytes) %> per result and <%= number_to_human_size(Assistant::Config.max_total_bytes) %> total result data.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3 lg:grid-cols-3">
        <label class="text-xs font-medium text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">
          Disabled exact tools
          <%= hidden_field_tag "settings[disabled_capability_tools][]", "" %>
          <%= select_tag "settings[disabled_capability_tools][]",
            options_for_select(capability_tools, setting.disabled_capability_tools),
            multiple: true, size: 10,
            class: "mt-1 block w-full rounded-md border-zinc-300 bg-white font-mono text-xs dark:border-zinc-700 dark:bg-zinc-950" %>
        </label>
        <label class="text-xs font-medium text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">
          Disabled effect classes
          <%= hidden_field_tag "settings[disabled_capability_effects][]", "" %>
          <%= select_tag "settings[disabled_capability_effects][]",
            options_for_select(capability_effects, setting.disabled_capability_effects),
            multiple: true, size: 10,
            class: "mt-1 block w-full rounded-md border-zinc-300 bg-white font-mono text-xs dark:border-zinc-700 dark:bg-zinc-950" %>
        </label>
        <label class="text-xs font-medium text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">
          Disabled modules
          <%= hidden_field_tag "settings[disabled_capability_modules][]", "" %>
          <%= select_tag "settings[disabled_capability_modules][]",
            options_for_select(capability_modules, setting.disabled_capability_modules),
            multiple: true, size: 10,
            class: "mt-1 block w-full rounded-md border-zinc-300 bg-white font-mono text-xs dark:border-zinc-700 dark:bg-zinc-950" %>
        </label>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <label class="text-sm text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">
        Transcript retention (days)
        <%= number_field_tag "settings[transcript_retention_days]", setting.transcript_retention_days,
          min: 1, max: 30, required: true,
          class: "mt-1 block w-full rounded-md border-zinc-300 bg-white dark:border-zinc-700 dark:bg-zinc-900" %>
      </label>
      <label class="text-sm text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">
        Security audit retention (days)
        <%= number_field_tag "settings[audit_retention_days]", setting.audit_retention_days,
          min: 1, max: 365, required: true,
          class: "mt-1 block w-full rounded-md border-zinc-300 bg-white dark:border-zinc-700 dark:bg-zinc-900" %>
      </label>
    </div>
    <div><%= submit_tag "Save assistant settings", class: "rounded-md bg-zinc-900 px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-white dark:bg-zinc-100 dark:text-zinc-900" %></div>
  <% end %>

  <div class="mt-6">
    <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100">Direct chat backends</h3>
    <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400">These backends are fixed, read-only application configuration. Each uses its own subscription login and isolated credential volume. API-key provider profiles are retired from new chat, and Hunter does not accept provider API keys here.</p>
    <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <article data-assistant-backend="codex" class="rounded-lg border border-zinc-200 p-4 dark:border-zinc-800">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="grid h-10 w-10 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-lg bg-zinc-950">
            <%= image_tag "assistant/openai.svg", alt: "", aria: { hidden: true }, class: "h-7 w-7 object-contain" %>
          </span>
          <div>
            <p class="font-medium text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100">OpenAI</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-zinc-500">Codex CLI direct backend</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-xs leading-5 text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Authenticate the isolated backend as an operator, then restart only that backend if needed:</p>
        <code class="mt-2 block overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-zinc-950 px-3 py-2 text-xs text-zinc-100">codex login --device-auth</code>
      </article>

      <article data-assistant-backend="claude_code" class="rounded-lg border border-zinc-200 p-4 dark:border-zinc-800">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="grid h-10 w-10 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-lg bg-zinc-950">
            <%= image_tag "assistant/anthropic.svg", alt: "", aria: { hidden: true }, class: "h-6 w-8 object-contain" %>
          </span>
          <div>
            <p class="font-medium text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100">Anthropic</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-zinc-500">Claude Code CLI direct backend</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-xs leading-5 text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Authenticate the isolated backend as an operator, then restart only that backend if needed:</p>
        <code class="mt-2 block overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-zinc-950 px-3 py-2 text-xs text-zinc-100">claude login</code>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-zinc-200 bg-zinc-50 p-4 text-xs leading-5 text-zinc-600 dark:border-zinc-800 dark:bg-zinc-900/50 dark:text-zinc-400">
    Provider subscriptions may retain data under their own policies. Hunter retains encrypted transcripts for the configured period above, while local deletion cannot erase provider or backup copies. Every Hunter feature, including future API-backed features, remains available to these backends only through the authenticated, per-turn-authorized Hunter MCP gateway. Codex may expose its pinned provider-owned internal utility and discovery tools inside its isolated read-only service; those tools have no direct Hunter or host access.
  </div>
</section>
